From: DeBeOS <noreply@debeos>
Subject: [PATCH] unix,haiku: implement the process title (proctitle.c + rename_thread)

Haiku built no-proctitle.c, so uv_set_process_title() was a no-op and
uv_get_process_title() always returned "". Node's process.title, --title,
the inspector's context name and the trace-events process_name all read it.
Use the generic argv-overwriting proctitle.c (Haiku passes argv strings
contiguously) and implement uv__set_process_title() by renaming the main
thread, whose id is the team id; the kernel's team_info.args (what ps shows)
cannot be changed from userland.
---
 CMakeLists.txt   | 2 +-
 Makefile.am      | 2 +-
 src/unix/haiku.c | 9 +++++++++
 3 files changed, 11 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/CMakeLists.txt b/CMakeLists.txt
--- a/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -417,7 +417,7 @@ if(CMAKE_SYSTEM_NAME STREQUAL "Haiku")
 	  src/unix/haiku.c
 	  src/unix/haiku-fsevents.c
 	  src/unix/bsd-ifaddrs.c
-	  src/unix/no-proctitle.c
+	  src/unix/proctitle.c
 	  src/unix/posix-hrtime.c
 	  src/unix/posix-poll.c)
 endif()
diff --git a/Makefile.am b/Makefile.am
--- a/Makefile.am
+++ b/Makefile.am
@@ -470,7 +470,7 @@ libuv_la_CFLAGS += -D_BSD_SOURCE
 libuv_la_SOURCES += src/unix/bsd-ifaddrs.c \
                     src/unix/haiku.c \
                     src/unix/haiku-fsevents.c \
-                    src/unix/no-proctitle.c \
+                    src/unix/proctitle.c \
                     src/unix/posix-hrtime.c \
                     src/unix/posix-poll.c
 test_run_tests_LDFLAGS += -lbsd
diff --git a/src/unix/haiku.c b/src/unix/haiku.c
--- a/src/unix/haiku.c
+++ b/src/unix/haiku.c
@@ -170,3 +170,12 @@ int uv_cpu_info(uv_cpu_info_t** cpu_infos, int* count) {
 
   return 0;
 }
+
+
+void uv__set_process_title(const char* title) {
+  /* Haiku keeps a team's command line in the kernel (team_info.args), which
+   * userland cannot change; what can be renamed is the main thread, whose id
+   * is the team id. That is the name the Debugger, ProcessController and
+   * `ps -a` show for the main thread. */
+  rename_thread(getpid(), title);
+}
